Dear ImGui is a bloat-free graphical user interface library for C++. It
outputs optimized vertex buffers that you can render anytime in your
3D-pipeline-enabled application. It is fast, portable, renderer agnostic,
and self-contained (no external dependencies).

This package builds it as libraries, static and shared, with pkg-config
files: libimgui (the core, the demo window and the std::string helpers)
and one library per back end: OpenGL 2 (fixed function), SDL2 (platform
and renderer) and GLFW. The back ends' sources are installed too, in
share/imgui/backends, for programs that compile their own.

ImWchar is 32 bits wide (IMGUI_USE_WCHAR32), so text beyond Unicode's
Basic Multilingual Plane, such as emoji, can be shown.
